# Scenario diag-stic2-border-pass (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05, D-10): outcome pass, exit 0. The program ivs-diag-stic-2 through the
# project boot stub contract 2 with the zero graphics ROM and KEY_2 closed from tick 0: the first read of 01FE returns the low
# byte BE, so the program writes scene 4 in every frame (one MOB under the corner and the border extension register at 0003,
# delay 0). The asserts are the hand-derived expectations of data/golden/diag-stic2-border-pass.expect (derivation in
# docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md, section (f), written before the program): the same lines in the same order as the
# committed block of that document, and the same as the .expect (golden-expect-drift). The idle control diag-stic2-idle-pass
# differs from this scenario in the video and input digests only (data/expected/scenario-pairs.ids). The hash and the probes are
# derived under the pinned defaults PD-8 and PD-9 (derivation, section (i)); the probes avoid the positions those pins move. It
# never halts.
ivss 1
id diag-stic2-border-pass
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub-2
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-stic-2.ivsc
capture video 0 10
input at_tick=0 c0=KEY_2 c1=0x0
run-to 640000 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000A
assert mem 02F2 == 00BE
assert mem 02F3 == 0004
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 5 displayed == yes
assert frame 5 hash == 49b089730cf6c3b17e52f9b6aea588a258c9c5a8c28139ff5e4045dc5f4f5fa2
assert frame 5 pixel 0 0 == 8
assert frame 5 pixel 100 3 == 8
assert frame 5 pixel 8 8 == 4
assert frame 5 pixel 8 12 == 1
assert video count == 10
